          ],
          "id": "c1",
          "value": {
            "language": "en",
            "text": "Azad Jammu and Kashmir Medical College (AJKMC) is a public medical institution in Muzaffarabad, Azad Jammu and Kashmir, Pakistan. Its English name is also presented as Azad Jammu Kashmir Medical College, and the institution is additionally identified as Mirwaiz Maulvi Mohammad Farooq Medical College. The college offers an MBBS program and the available encyclopedia account describes a student body of approximately 500, without a specified statistical year.\n\nThe college's establishment date is reported inconsistently: Wikidata and the encyclopedia infobox give 2012, while the article narrative says it was established in 2011. The narrative separately dates its inauguration to 8 October 2011 by Prime Minister Syed Yousaf Raza Gillani. It connects the rationale for establishing the college to shortages of medical professionals highlighted by the 2005 Kashmir earthquake. Clinical rotations for its MBBS students are described at Combined Military Hospital Muzaffarabad and Abbas Institute of Medical Sciences. The article lists professional recognition and affiliations, including the Pakistan Medical and Dental Council and the University of Azad Jammu and Kashmir. It also identifies the Kashmir Journal of Medical Sciences as the college's scientific journal."
          },
          "verification": "supported"
        }
